PS+=['When we go to the beach, sometimes we will see hermit crabs on the beach. And we all know hermit crabs have to change to bigger shells when they grow bigger. In fact, when they finally find a new shell, they have a special habit: They will tell other hermit crabs to change shells together!\nHow do they change shells together? When they start to get together, they will stand in line according to their sizes. After the first one (also the biggest one) takes off its shell, the second 【one】 (smaller than the biggest one) puts on the shell of the first one. Then the third one puts on the shell of the second one, and so on. It is interesting, isn’t it?\nWhy do they change shells this way? In fact, it is not easy to find a new shell. By doing this, the chance of not finding a shell will be smaller. Hermit crabs try their best to live. To help them, please don’t take away shells on the beach, and don’t leave trash on the beach, either. Don’t make them only have to live by taking our trash as their homes.\n（hermit crab 寄居蟹　shell 殼　according to 根據）']
