PS+=['A lost dog walks into a jungle. A lion sees him from far away and thinks, “I never saw this kind of animal before, and he looks weak. Maybe I can eat him for lunch.” So the lion starts running to the dog. The dog notices that and is afraid. Then he sees some bones next to him and comes up with an idea. He says loudly, “Hmm... ＿38＿!”\nThe lion hears this and stops. He thinks, “Wow, this guy is so much stronger than I ＿39＿. I should leave before he gets me.”\nIn the tree a monkey sees everything. He thinks if he tells the lion the truth, he ＿40＿ something good from the lion. So the monkey goes to tell the lion what really happened right away. The lion is angry and says, “Get on my back. We’ll get him together!”\nThey start running to the dog again. The dog sees that and gets even more scared. Then he comes up with another idea and shouts angrily, “＿41＿ I told him to bring me another lion one hour ago!” The lion hears that and feels more afraid. Quickly he runs away with the monkey on his back just like that, even without time to think of the idea that he should teach the monkey a good lesson.\n（jungle 叢林　bone 骨頭　truth 事實）']
